  "id": "biological-perspective",
  "term": "biological perspective",
  "definition": "In this source, a biological perspective means understanding identification by its function in living organisms, especially how animals signal who they are and recognize particular individuals over time and across places. It treats identification as biologically important for both the sender and the receiver of signals.",
